      "message": "refetchOnMount: false combined with onSuccess: () \u003d\u003e queryClient.invalidateQueries(...) creates a silent staleness trap. After a successful reboot POST, invalidateQueries marks the cached Manager as stale. If the user navigates away and back without a full page reload, refetchOnMount: false prevents the stale entry from being re-fetched on the next mount. The LastResetTime displayed will be the pre-reboot value.\n\nrefetchOnMount: false means \"never refetch on mount, even if the query is stale.\" Since the only mechanism to update LastResetTime after a reboot is the post-reboot invalidateQueries + a subsequent fetch, disabling mount-triggered refetches breaks the update path for in-session re-navigation.\n\nRecommendation:\nChange to refetchOnMount: true (the TanStack Query default). When staleTime: Infinity data is fresh it won\u0027t refetch anyway; when it has been invalidated (marked stale by onSuccess), it will refetch on the next mount:\n\n```\nrefetchOnMount: true,   // was: false\n```",
