      "side": 1,
      "message": "Issue:\nstartLoader() is called unconditionally, then the watcher fires with { immediate: true }. If useRedfishRoot() hasn\u0027t resolved yet when this page mounts (i.e., empty cache on first visit), managersCollectionUri is null, so bmcQuery.enabled is false. A disabled TanStack Query reports isLoading \u003d false. The immediate watcher therefore fires endLoader() synchronously — before any data is fetched — hiding the loading bar immediately after startLoader() shows it.\n\n\nTanStack Query v5 defines isLoading as true only when the query has no data and is actively fetching. A disabled query (enabled: false) always reports isLoading: false. The watcher cannot distinguish \"disabled, waiting for pre-req\" from \"done loading\".\n\nRecommendation:\nWatch both bmcQuery.isLoading and the intermediary useRedfishRoot().isLoading together, or derive a composite isPageLoading ref:\n\n\n```\nconst { isLoading: rootLoading } \u003d useRedfishRoot();\nconst isPageLoading \u003d computed(\n  () \u003d\u003e rootLoading.value || bmcQuery.isLoading.value,\n);\n\nstartLoader();\nwatch(isPageLoading, (loading) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (!loading) endLoader();\n}, { immediate: true });\n```",
